<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jind Kaur</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1817">1817</a>–<a href="/years/1863">1863</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Maharani Jind Kaur, Rani Jindan</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jind Kaur was the youngest wife of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ranjit-singh">Maharaja Ranjit Singh</a> and mother of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/duleep-singh">Duleep Singh</a>, the last ruler of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sikh-empire">Sikh Empire</a>. She acted as regent for her young son from 1843, and after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-anglo-sikh-war">First Anglo-Sikh War</a> the British removed her from power, imprisoned and exiled her. She escaped to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nepal">Nepal</a> in 1849, was reunited with her son in 1861 and died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a> in 1863.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jind-kaur.jpg" alt="Jind Kaur" width="320" height="436" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: George Richmond · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Maharani_Jind_Kaur.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Sher Singh was assassinated in 1843, along with the chief minister Dhian Singh, and the five-year-old Duleep Singh was installed under the regency of his mother, <b>Maharani Jind Kaur</b>.</blockquote><a href="/empire/sikh-empire">Sikh Empire · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in Gujranwala, in what is now <a href="/countries/pakistan">Pakistan</a>. Died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/united-kingdom">the United Kingdom</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=32.15,74.18&amp;year=1846" aria-label="Gujranwala on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6458 994 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Jind Kaur"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6908 1264h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6908 1264h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=32.15,74.18&amp;year=1846">What was here in 1846? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
